"""Brings a machine to what nodes/ holds for it: its name, UTC, the files that make Docker wait for
/data, SSH's local forwarding, the egress proxy, the firewall, apt's units on Debian, apk's door on
Alpine, and what the relay peer and host read. Run again it changes nothing. See
spec/architecture/nodes.md.

`node host <name>` starts the first host on a node set up that way and hands it a CI run, from
which host deploys the rest. See spec/architecture/host.md, "The machine pulls; nothing pushes
into it".

`node <verb> <name>` asks that node's host over SSH, for the verbs host_api.py lists."""

